    "Sign in" : {

    },
    "Sign in with an AT Protocol identity, like your Bluesky account, to let people pay you at your handle. You sign in on your account host's own page, and Avocadough only asks for permission to manage its payment address record." : {

    },
    "Sign in with your handle" : {

    },
    "Sign out" : {

    },
    "Sign-in service" : {

    },
    "Sign-in was cancelled" : {

    },
    "Signed in as" : {

    },
    "Signing in with an AT Protocol identity, such as a Bluesky account, is optional. You sign in on your account host’s own page, so Avocadough never sees your password. Signing in gives the app access tokens, which it keeps in the device Keychain, and the only permission it asks for is to manage its own payment address record in your account.\n\nIf you publish a payment address, Avocadough writes a public record to your AT Protocol account that links your handle to your wallet’s Lightning address. Anyone can read that record. It stays in place until you unpublish it in the app, including after you sign out or delete the app." : {

